   "Praca zdalna oznaczona w 1,7% ofert"
  ],
  "caveats_pl": "Dane obejmują tylko oferty pracy z internetu z 3 serwisów i są zbierane od 1 sierpnia 2026 r., więc brak porównań w czasie, a mediana wynagrodzenia dotyczy 51% ogłoszeń z podaną kwotą.",
  "lead_en": "Online job postings in the US are dispersed: in August 2026 they came from 37,097 cities, and the largest, Houston, accounted for 0.9% of postings.",
  "body_en": "In August 2026 we collected 3,986,696 new online job postings in the United States. This figure excludes duplicates across services. Before deduplication there were 4,964,099 postings, and an estimated 19.7% appeared on more than one service. At the end of the month 3,527,348 postings were active. The data come from 3 aggregators: Indeed (2,851,035 postings, 57.4%), Careerjet (1,466,605) and Jooble (646,459).\n\nThe median salary was 5,000 USD per month. Half of the stated pay fell between 3,467 and 8,192 USD. 51% of postings stated an amount, and these figures refer only to them.\n\nPostings are spread across 37,097 cities. The most were in Houston (46,028), Chicago (38,359), Atlanta (36,894), New York (34,712) and Dallas (33,738). None of these cities exceeds 1% of postings. 1.7% of postings were marked as remote. Full-time was stated in 32.5% of postings, part-time in 12.9% and contract in 2.9%. 51.3% did not state the employment type.\n\nAugust is the first complete month of data collection. Earlier months are incomplete, so we do not report month-on-month or year-on-year changes.",
